hat position. He can jump onto the block? The block top is at y 144 (the used block). Mario big top at 176. Hmm, the flower is at y 132-147, which is above the block top (144). Actually the block is at y 144-159; the flower at 132-147 overlaps the top. So the flower sits on top of the block. Mario would need to be standing on the block (y top = 144-32 = 112 for big Mario?) Hmm big Mario standing on the block top (144) → his top at 112. Then the flower at 132-147 would overlap him. But how to get him onto the block? Jump from the ground: he can jump up and land on the block if he moves horizontally. \n\nSimpler: teleport Mario to the flower's position: set $006D/$0086 = flower x (183+256?) and $00CE = 130. Then step a frame → collision → collect. Let me do that.\n\nActually, the flower's level x: screen 183 + camera 153 = 336. So level x=336. Mario abs 343 currently. Set $006D=1, $0086=80 (336), $00CE=132, $00B5=1. Step a frame or two. Then check $0756/$0755 for fire state and Mario's palette.\n\nHmm, but setting Mario's y to 132 (floating) and x under the flower: the flower is at level 336-351, and Mario at 336 → overlap. Collision should trigger.\n\nAlternatively, just make Mario jump again while moving slightly left/right onto the block. But teleport is easier.\n\nActually, even simpler: I can use the fact that Mario is big and standing under the block; if he jumps and I move him left onto the block... hmm.\n\nLet me just teleport. But first, record the flower mapping while it's on screen (the game is paused; but a write would change state; recording doesn't change state). Let me do palette reads + record now.\n\nLet me call get_all_palettes and get_pixel_color(187,134)."}
