{"type":"text","text":"Both sprites are named, proven with `list_sprites`, recorded, and promoted (mapping file now has 7 sprites).\n\n## 1. `fire_flower` — the fire flower\n\nReached by restarting World 1-1 fresh, making Mario big (`$0756`=1), and jumping into the left ? block of the brick row. Because Mario was big, that mushroom block yielded a **fire flower** instead of a mushroom — the flower rose out of the used block.\n\n`list_sprites` on it (paused, origin (183,132), 16×16, all **sprite palette 5** = `[$0F, $1A green, $30 white, $27 orange]`, all behind-background):\n\n| OAM tile | offset | flips | role |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `$D6` | +0,+0 | none | upper-left (petals + orange centre) |\n| `$D6` | +8,+0 | flip_h | upper-right |\n| `$D9` | +0,+8 | none | lower-left (green stem/leaves) |\n| `$D9` | +8,+8 | flip_h | lower-right |\n\nThe art is symmetric, so only 2 distinct CHR tiles are drawn once plain and once mirrored. Verified by pixel: `$27` orange on the head at (187,136).\n\n## 2. `fireball` — Fire Mario's fireball\n\nCollecting the flower took `$0756` from 1 → 2 (fire). Pressing **B** spawned the ball; `list_sprites` caught it mid-flight:\n\n- **sample A:** single 8×8 OAM entry, tile `$65`, (226,200), attr `$02` → **sprite palette 6** = `[$0F, $16 red, $30 white, $27 orange]`, no flips.\n- **sample B (5 frames later):** tile `$64`, (246,191), attr `$C2` → same palette, flipped both ways.\n\nSo it's one tile (not a multi-tile metasprite), moving ~+4 px/frame right, bouncing, cycling the rotation tiles `$64`–`$67`. Verified by pixel: `$16` red at (229,203); `read_tile $65` is a round ball (red outline, orange body, white highlight).\n\nAlso noted in passing: Mario's power byte is `$0756` (0=small, 1=big, 2=fire; `$D820`/`$D82D` sets 2). The emulator is paused with the fireball on screen if you want a look."}
